# Page objects

## 1. Where locators live

Locators and actions belong in `tests/pages`. Specs import page objects and only describe the flow and assert.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/BrowsePage.ts + tests/e2e/browse.spec.ts
this.sortBy = page.getByLabel('Sort by');
await browse.sortPriceHighToLow();
await expect(browse.firstPlantHeading).toHaveText(/* … */);

// ❌ BAD — locator built in the spec
await page.getByLabel('Sort by').selectOption({ label: 'Price: high to low' });
```

## 2. Locator order

Prefer `getByRole`, then `getByLabel`, then `getByText`. Never CSS or XPath. An control with no accessible name (F-07 heart) is found by role inside its card, with a comment that names the finding.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/BrowsePage.ts
// F-07: Save (heart) button has no accessible name — find by role inside its card.
return this.plantCard(plantName).getByRole('button');

// ❌ BAD
page.locator('.save');
page.locator('//button[contains(@class,"save")]');
```

## 3. Actions return nothing or the next page object

Async actions perform a user step and return `void` or the page that follows. They never assert.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/CartPage.ts / RegisterPage.ts
async goToCheckout(): Promise<CheckoutPage> {
  await this.goToCheckoutLink.click();
  return new CheckoutPage(this.page);
}
async createAccount(/* … */): Promise<BrowsePage> { /* fill, click, return new BrowsePage */ }

// ❌ BAD — assert inside the page object / return a boolean snapshot
async goToCheckout(): Promise<void> {
  await this.goToCheckoutLink.click();
  await expect(this.page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Checkout' })).toBeVisible();
}
```

## 4. Assertions stay in the spec

Every `expect` lives in `tests/e2e` (or visual specs). Page objects expose locators; specs keep the same assertions.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — tests/e2e/plant-reviews.spec.ts
await expect(plant.thanksToast).toBeVisible();
await expect(plant.reviewsRegion).toContainText(reviewText);

// ❌ BAD — expectation hidden in PlantPage
async postReviewAndExpectThanks(): Promise<void> {
  await this.postReviewButton.click();
  await expect(this.thanksToast).toBeVisible();
}
```
